AFS(1)

NAME
       afs - the Enterprise Agent Factory Service command line

SYNOPSIS
       afs [options] <service> <operation> [parameters]

SERVICES
       admin            Service administration: settings, templates, tags, channels, storage and security operators.
       agents           Create and operate agents, their identities, configuration and external systems.
       api-keys         Create and revoke API keys.
       audit            Search and export the audit log.
       budgets          Set budgets and read spend.
       collaboration    
       completion       Print a shell completion script.
       configure        Create and edit profiles in ~/.afs/config.
       members          Manage team members and role bindings.
       models           List and manage models and their prices.
       pools            Manage worker pools.
       reports          Run and schedule reports.
       secrets          Manage secret references and write secret values.
       sso              Sign in with single sign-on and show who you are.
       swarm-templates  Manage swarm templates.
       teams            Create and manage teams.
       work-orders      Manage work orders and their repositories.

GLOBAL OPTIONS
       --profile                Use a specific profile from ~/.afs/config.
       --endpoint-url           Override the API endpoint URL.
       --output                 Output format: json, yaml, table, text or csv.
       --query                  JMESPath query applied to the result before rendering.
       --no-paginate            Return only the first page of results.
       --max-items              Stop after this many items and print NextToken.
       --page-size              Items per request (maxResults), 1 to 100.
       --starting-token         Resume from a NextToken printed by --max-items.
       --cli-input-json         Read parameters from a JSON document or file://path.
       --generate-cli-skeleton  Print a JSON skeleton of the input and make no call.
       --debug                  Write a redacted request log to stderr.
       --no-cli-pager           Do not send output through a pager.
       --color                  Colored output: on, off or auto.
       --cli-connect-timeout    Connect timeout in seconds (0 for none; default 30).
       --cli-read-timeout       Read timeout in seconds (0 for none; default 60).
       --version                Print the afs version and exit.

To see help text for a service, run: afs <service> help
